:: Start [nobar]
<<include "Banner">>
<div class="stamp">Case file 004</div>
<p class="meta">A library archive · London · today</p>
<h1>The Tower Ledger</h1>
<p>The archivist leads you down to a quiet reading room and sets a heavy box on the table. Inside: copies of old letters, laws, histories and reports, some more than 500 years old.</p>
<p class="quote chief">"Two princes. One tower. 1483. Everyone has an opinion, and most of them got it from a play. I want yours, built on the sources. Mind who wrote each one, and when. Seven leads."</p>
<div class="how">
<p><b>How to investigate</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Visiting a new shelf uses one lead. Going back is free.</li>
<li>Put the sources in the order they were written on the <b>ledger board</b>. Connect clues on the <b>deduction board</b>. Both are free.</li>
<li>Before your verdict, you'll mark each key source: written at the time, written later, or modern.</li>
<li><b>This case has no answer key.</b> "We can't tell yet" is a real verdict.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="actions">[[Open the box|Hub]]</div>


:: Hub
<<if $leads lte 0>><<goto "OutOfLeads">><</if>>
<h2>Which shelf?</h2>
<p class="meta">New shelves cost a lead. Shelves you've visited are free to revisit.</p>
<<casemap>>
<details class="maplist"><summary>Show the places as a list</summary>
<ul class="map">
<li><<maplink "Tower" "🏰 The Tower of London guidebook">></li>
<li><<maplink "Mancini" "📜 An Italian visitor's report, 1483">></li>
<li><<maplink "Law" "📜 Parliament's records, 1484">></li>
<li><<maplink "More" "📖 Thomas More's history">></li>
<li><<maplink "Suspects" "👑 The suspects shelf">></li>
<li><<maplink "Warbeck" "✉️ The pretender's file">></li>
<li><<maplink "Bones" "⚱️ The 1674 discovery">></li>
<li><<maplink "Exam" "🔬 The 1933 examination">></li>
<li><<maplink "Langley" "📚 The 2023 research">></li>
<li><<maplink "Giftshop" "🛍️ The museum gift shop">></li>
</ul>
</details>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Ledger board (free)">><<set $return to "Hub">><<goto "Ledger">><</link>><<link "Deduction board (free)">><<set $return to "Hub">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[I'm ready to decide|Sort]]</div>


:: OutOfLeads
<h2>Out of leads</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"The library's closing," the archivist says. "Your verdict?"</p>
<div class="actions"><<link "One last look at the ledger board">><<set $return to "OutOfLeads">><<goto "Ledger">><</link>><<link "One last look at the deduction board">><<set $return to "OutOfLeads">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[Make your call|Sort]]</div>


:: Ledger
<h2>Ledger board</h2>
<p class="meta">Tap the sources in the order they were written, oldest first. You can only place sources you've found. If one couldn't come next, the board will tell you.</p>
<div id="lgboard"><<include "LedgerCards">></div>
<div class="actions"><<link "Back">><<goto $return>><</link>></div>


:: LedgerCards
<<set _have to setup.ledger.filter(function(t){ return $notebook.includes(t.need); })>>
<<set _left to _have.filter(function(t){ return !$lg.includes(t.id); }).sort(function(a,b){ return a.text.localeCompare(b.text); })>>
<h3>Your ledger so far</h3>
<<if $lg.length is 0>><p class="slot-empty">Nothing placed yet.</p>
<<else>><ol class="timeline"><<for _id range $lg>><li><<print setup.ledger.find(function(t){ return t.id === _id; }).text>></li><</for>></ol><</if>>
<<if $lmsg isnot "">><p class="note warn" role="status"><<print $lmsg>></p><</if>>
<<if _have.length is 0>><p class="note">You haven't found any sources yet.</p>
<<elseif _left.length gt 0>>
<h3>Place next</h3>
<div class="choices">
<<for _t range _left>><<capture _t>><span class="opt"><<link _t.text>>
<<set _next to _have.filter(function(h){ return !$lg.includes(h.id); }).sort(function(a,b){ return setup.ledger.indexOf(a) - setup.ledger.indexOf(b); })[0]>>
<<if _t.id is _next.id>><<run $lg.push(_t.id)>><<set $lmsg to "">>
<<else>><<set $lmiss to $lmiss + 1>><<set $lmsg to "Not yet. Something you've found was written before that. Check the dates.">><</if>>
<<replace "#lgboard">><<include "LedgerCards">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>>
</div>
<<else>><p class="note">Every source you've found is placed.</p><</if>>
<p class="meta">Sources placed: <<print $lg.length>> of <<print _have.length>> found · Wrong tries: <<print $lmiss>></p>


:: Tower
<h2>The Tower of London guidebook</h2>
<p>A thick guidebook with a map of the Tower: walls, towers, the great White Tower in the middle, and the royal rooms.</p>
<<clue "palace">>
<<clue "control">>
<<tomap>>


:: Mancini
<h2>An Italian visitor's report</h2>
<<include "Scene">>
<p>A copy of a report by Dominic Mancini, an Italian who was in London in the spring and summer of 1483. He finished it before the end of that year.</p>
<<clue "mancini">>
<<tomap>>


:: Law
<h2>Parliament's records</h2>
<p>A copy of a long law in old-fashioned English, from early 1484.</p>
<<clue "titulus">>
<<clue "neverShown">>
<<tomap>>


:: More
<h2>Thomas More's history</h2>
<p>A printed history of Richard III, and next to it, a copy of a famous play.</p>
<<clue "more">>
<<clue "play">>
<<tomap>>


:: Suspects
<h2>The suspects shelf</h2>
<p>Three folders: the uncle who became king, his powerful ally, and the man who took the crown from him.</p>
<<clue "buckDoc">>
<<clue "buckAccess">>
<<clue "henry">>
<<tomap>>


:: Warbeck
<h2>The pretender's file</h2>
<p>Letters from foreign courts, and a confession.</p>
<<clue "warbeck">>
<<clue "confession">>
<<tomap>>


:: Bones
<h2>The 1674 discovery</h2>
<p>A drawing of an old staircase, and a note about an urn designed for Westminster Abbey.</p>
<<clue "bones">>
<<clue "urn">>
<<tomap>>


:: Exam
<h2>The 1933 examination</h2>
<p>A scientific report with photographs of measuring tools.</p>
<<clue "exam">>
<<clue "nodna">>
<<tomap>>


:: Langley
