<<clue "swap">>
<<tomap>>


:: Sort [nobar]
<<set _pool to setup.sortOrder.filter(function(id){ return $notebook.includes(id); }).slice(0, 6)>>
<div class="stamp">Sort the sources</div>
<h2>When was it written?</h2>
<p>For each key source, decide: was it <b>written at the time</b> (1483 to the 1490s), <b>written later</b> (decades or centuries later), or <b>modern</b> (the last hundred years)?</p>
<<if _pool.length is 0>><p class="note">You don't have any key sources to sort. You'll go straight to your verdict.</p>
<<else>><div id="sortlist"><<include "SortList">></div><</if>>
<div class="actions">[[On to my verdict|Accusation]]</div>


:: SortList
<<set _pool to setup.sortOrder.filter(function(id){ return $notebook.includes(id); }).slice(0, 6)>>
<<for _id range _pool>><<capture _id>>
<div class="sortrow"><p class="card-title"><<print setup.cards[_id].title>></p>
<div class="choices three"><<for _k range ["time","later","modern"]>><<capture _k>><span @class="$sort[_id] is _k ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link setup.kindLabel[_k]>><<set $sort[_id] to _k>><<replace "#sortlist">><<include "SortList">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div></div>
<</capture>><</for>>


:: Accusation [nobar]
<div class="stamp">Verdict</div>
<h2>"What happened to the princes?"</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"Your verdict, how sure you are, and up to three sources that back it up."</p>
<h3>1. Your verdict</h3>
<div id="verdicts"><<include "VerdictList">></div>
<h3>2. How sure are you?</h3>
<div id="confs"><<include "ConfList">></div>
<h3>3. Pin up to 3 cards as evidence</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">Your notebook is empty.</p>
<<else>><div id="pins"><<include "PinList">></div><</if>>
<div id="file"><<include "FileButton">></div>


:: VerdictList
<<set _opts to [["richard","Richard III was responsible"],["buck","The Duke of Buckingham was responsible"],["henry","Henry VII was responsible"],["survived","They survived"],["unknown","We can't tell yet"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$verdict is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $verdict to _o[0]>><<replace "#verdicts">><<include "VerdictList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "FileButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: ConfList
<<set _opts to [["hunch","Just a hunch"],["fairly","Fairly sure"],["very","Very sure"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$conf is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $conf to _o[0]>><<replace "#confs">><<include "ConfList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "FileButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: PinList
<p class="meta">Pinned: <<print $pinned.length>> of 3. Tap a card to pin or unpin it.</p>
<div class="cards pinboard">
<<for _id range $notebook>><<capture _id>><span @class="($pinned.includes(_id) ? 'opt pinned' : 'opt') + (setup.cards[_id].type === 'deduction' ? ' ded' : '')"><<link setup.cards[_id].title>><<if $pinned.includes(_id)>><<run $pinned.delete(_id)>><<elseif $pinned.length lt 3>><<run $pinned.push(_id)>><</if>><<replace "#pins">><<include "PinList">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>>
</div>


:: FileButton
<<if $verdict is "" or $conf is "">><p class="note">Choose a verdict and how sure you are.</p>
<<else>><div class="actions">[[File my verdict|Verdict]]</div><</if>>


:: Verdict [nobar]
<<set _have to setup.ledger.filter(function(t){ return $notebook.includes(t.need); })>>
<<set _s1 to $lg.length gte 5 and $lg.length is _have.length and $lmiss lte 2>>
<<set _pool to setup.sortOrder.filter(function(id){ return $notebook.includes(id); }).slice(0, 6)>>
<<set $sortRight to _pool.filter(function(id){ return $sort[id] === setup.cards[id].type; }).length>>
<<set _s2 to _pool.length gte 3 and $sortRight gte _pool.length - 1>>
<<set _leans to $pinned.map(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].lean; })>>
<<set _nG to $pinned.filter(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "assumption"; }).length>>
<<set _distinct to _leans.filter(function(x, i){ return x !== "neither" && _leans.indexOf(x) === i; }).length>>
<<if $verdict is "unknown">><<set _s3 to _distinct gte 2 and _nG is 0>>
<<else>><<set _s3 to _leans.filter(function(x){ return x === $verdict; }).length gte 2 and _nG is 0>><</if>>
<<if $verdict is "unknown">><<set _s4 to $conf isnot "very">>
<<elseif $conf is "very">><<set _s4 to false>>
<<elseif $conf is "fairly">><<set _s4 to _s3>>
<<else>><<set _s4 to true>><</if>>
<<set $stars to (_s1 ? 1 : 0) + (_s2 ? 1 : 0) + (_s3 ? 1 : 0) + (_s4 ? 1 : 0)>>
<<set $deductions to $notebook.filter(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "deduction"; }).length>>
<<switch $verdict>>
<<case "richard">><div class="stamp">Verdict: Richard III</div>
<<case "buck">><div class="stamp">Verdict: Buckingham</div>
<<case "henry">><div class="stamp">Verdict: Henry VII</div>
<<case "survived">><div class="stamp">Verdict: they survived</div>
<<default>><div class="stamp solved">Verdict: can't tell yet</div>
<</switch>>
<h2>Detective rating: <<print $stars>> of 4 stars</h2>
<p class="meta">Nobody knows the true answer, so these stars measure how well you used the sources, not whether you "won."</p>
<ul class="stars">
<li @class="_s1 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s1 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>The ledger.</b> <<if _s1>>Your sources are in the order they were written.<<elseif $lg.length lt 5>>You placed <<print $lg.length>> sources. Find and place at least five.<<elseif $lg.length lt _have.length>>Some sources you found are still off the ledger.<<else>>All placed, but it took <<print $lmiss>> wrong tries. Check each date before you tap.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s2 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s2 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>At the time, or later?</b> <<if _pool.length lt 3>>You didn't find enough key sources to sort.<<else>>You sorted <<print $sortRight>> of <<print _pool.length>> correctly.<<if not _s2>> Ask: was the writer alive and nearby in 1483?<</if>><</if>></li>
<li @class="_s3 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s3 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Evidence that fits your verdict.</b> <<if _s3>>The cards you pinned back up what you said.<<elseif _nG gt 0>>You pinned a gift-shop story. That's not evidence.<<elseif $verdict is "unknown">>For "can't tell yet," pin cards that point in at least two different directions.<<else>>Pin at least two cards that point toward your verdict.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s4 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s4 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Confidence that fits the evidence.</b> <<if $conf is "very" and $verdict isnot "unknown">>After 540 years, with untested bones and sources written for kings, "very sure" is too sure.<<elseif $verdict is "unknown" and $conf is "very">>Very sure nobody can tell? Fair, but "fairly sure" fits better.<<elseif _s4>>Your confidence matches how strong your evidence is.<<else>>"Fairly sure" needs pinned evidence that backs you up. Otherwise it's a hunch.<</if>></li>
</ul>
<p class="meta">Deductions worked out: <<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></p>
<h3>Your notebook, flipped over</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">You didn't collect any cards.</p><<else>>
<div class="cards reveal"><<for _id range $notebook>><<set _c to setup.cards[_id]>><div @class="'card ' + (_c.type === 'deduction' ? 'deduction' : _c.type === 'assumption' ? 'assumption' : 'evidence')"><span class="tag"><<print setup.kindLabel[_c.type]>><<if _c.type isnot "assumption">> · <<print setup.leanLabel[_c.lean]>><</if>></span><span class="card-title"><<print _c.title>></span><<if $pinned.includes(_id)>><span class="pinned-mark">You pinned this</span><</if>></div><</for>></div><</if>>
<div class="actions">[[What's known today|RealHistory]]</div>


:: RealHistory [nobar]
<h2>What's known today</h2>
<p>Most historians think Richard III was most likely responsible: the boys were in his care, they stood between him and the crown, and he never showed them alive. But the only report written at the time admits it didn't know what happened, and the most famous account was written decades later, while the kings who replaced him ruled.</p>
<p>The bones in Westminster Abbey have never been tested with DNA. In 2023 and 2025, new research argued the boys survived, and historians are still debating it.</p>
<p>More than 540 years later, the case is still open.</p>
<div class="lesson">
<h3>Your lesson as a trainee</h3>
<ul>
<li>Ask who wrote it, when, and who they were writing for.</li>
<li>A report from the time beats a story told decades later.</li>
<li>Old cases can stay open forever, and that's OK.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p class="note">Made up for this game: the archivist and the gift-shop stories. The sources, dates, people and the bones are real.</p>
<div class="actions">[[Finish case|CaseClosed]]</div>


:: CaseClosed [nobar]
<<include "Banner">>
<<run setup.reportResult()>>
<div class="stamp solved big">Case closed</div>
<h2>Case 004 complete</h2>
<p>Detective rating: <b><<print $stars>> of 4</b>. Deductions: <b><<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></b>.</p>
<div class="tellrocky">Go back to Rocky and type <b>done</b>.</div>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>></div>


